---
Always run the speckit skill workflow before implementing new features. Start with `speckit.specify` to create a spec, then `speckit.plan`, then `speckit.tasks`, then `speckit.implement`.

**Why:** User explicitly requires speckit for feature work in this project.

**How to apply:** When the user asks to implement a feature or fix that warrants a worktree/branch, invoke speckit.specify first rather than jumping straight to code changes.
---
name: Always use nix develop devshell for cargo commands
description: Never run cargo directly from nix store paths; always use nix develop --command
type: feedback
originSessionId: 91fe2faf-d0ee-4ecc-a569-78e104380eb4
---
Always run cargo via `nix develop --command cargo ...` — never use raw nix store paths like `/nix/store/.../cargo`.

**Why:** The nix devshell sets up the full Rust toolchain (rustc + std + linker) correctly. Using a bare cargo binary from the store without the matching std library causes "can't find crate for `core`" errors.

**How to apply:** Any time cargo needs to run (check, build, test, fmt, clippy, generate-lockfile), prefix with `nix develop --command`.

